WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.840
Armed conflict has cut crop land area by an average of 3% in exposed regions, with losses persisting for years. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 208. Researchers at the University of Cambridge examined previously unpublished notebooks from Rosalind Franklin dated 1952. The notes detail her recognition that DNA forms a double helix with specific base pairing before Watson and Crick published their model. Franklin described the anti-parallel strands and the role of hydrogen bonds between

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:36.840
bases. The documents also record her measurements of the helical pitch at 3.4 angstroms. Historians

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.940
note the notes add direct evidence of her independent insight into the structure. A team from

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:47.940
the Chinese Academy of Sciences combined 30-meter resolution cropland maps from 2000 to 2020

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:55.600
with over 460,000 geo-reference conflict events. They applied differences and propensity score matching

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:59.040
to isolate conflict effects within 5-kilometer buffers.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:06.900
Conflict zones showed an average 3.01 percent drop in crop land area, equal to 14.46 hectares

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.460
lost per buffer each year.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:14.300
Losses continued for multiple years after fighting began and reached 23.7 percent greater

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.140
than matched non-conflict areas.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:21.160
Western and Eastern Africa, plus Southeast Asia, recorded the largest declines.

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:23.320
The study appears in Nature Food.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:29.520
Researchers at Umeo University tested Microsoft HoloLens headsets that overlay digital information

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.180
in officers' fields of view.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:36.380
The system uses eye movements and voice commands to identify objects and potential risks

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:37.360
during interventions.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:43.100
Trials with police education programs in Sweden and Catalonia produce positive feedback on

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:43.920
decision support.

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:49.200
The work published in the Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research stresses that human

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.840
autonomy and ethical review must stay central.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.760
Collaboration between computing scientists and police researchers shaped the responsible

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:57.300
design.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:02.900
A University of Hong Kong team examined 50 physical card packs across popular games and

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:03.260
brands.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:09.520
Only 20% disclosed any probability information, and none listed the exact percentage chance

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:10.940
for every individual card.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:16.460
The study published in the Journal of Behavioral Addictions notes that consumer law in many

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:21.080
jurisdictions already requires such disclosures for similar random reward products.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:25.620
Higher-priced collector packs that can contain cards where thousands of dollars have

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:26.520
appeared recently.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:32.120
Researchers at the University of Alicante ran a year-long intervention in two Spanish schools

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:34.580
with 77 sixth grade students.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:41.120
The experimental group of 31 red picture books, poems, comics, and novel excerpts featuring

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.700
same-sex couples and gender diverse characters.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:48.840
researchers. The control group followed the standard curriculum. Post-intervention questionnaires

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:55.060
showed the experimental group had zero rejection of having a lesbian or gay friend, while 6.5%

00:02:55.060 --> 00:03:00.860
of the control group expressed reluctance. The study appears in education sciences. University

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:06.280
of Miami researchers reviewed internal National Catillmen's Association documents from 1986

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:13.180
to 1996. The records show the group attended an EPA workshop on livestock methane in February

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:17.960
1989, and learned of feeding and manure management options to cut emissions.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:23.360
Instead of pursuing reductions, the association questioned warming science and countered calls

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.320
to eat less beef.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:27.820
The study was published October 7 in Pios Climate.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:32.880
Lund University analysts reviewed reporting from the world's largest companies and sectors

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.780
with heavy biodiversity effects.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:39.320
Just 9% used formal biodiversity indicators to guide decisions.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:44.000
different indicators often produce conflicting conclusions about the same operations.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.540
The researchers issued seven recommendations for consistent indicator use.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:53.480
For decades, interferon tau was considered essential for maintaining cattle pregnancy

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.300
by signaling the embryo's presence.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:00.220
New experiments show cows can carry pregnancies to term and deliver healthy calves

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.160
even when this protein is absent.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:07.780
The finding challenges the long-standing model of maternal recognition of pregnancy in ruminants.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:13.580
A chance social media image led botanists to describe Victoria Columbiana, the fourth known

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:14.840
species in the genus.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:16.960
Its pads reach 2 meters across.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:20.060
The formal description appears in Phytotaxa.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:25.340
University of reading scientists reviewed 22 experimental studies on ozone and nitrogen

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:26.040
oxides.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:31.640
Both pollutants degrade or alter floral scent compounds, making it harder for bees and moths

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:32.720
to locate flowers.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:36.060
The combined effect is stronger than either pollutant alone.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:41.680
A University of Twentelead report for the Climate Research Initiative Netherlands identifies

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:46.700
ecological and social preconditions for responsible carbon dioxide removal at scale.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:52.960
The analysis covers land use change, biodiversity, water demand, and community acceptance.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:58.960
Two weeks after launch, the Copernicus Sentinel-3 satellite delivered initial data from its ocean

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:03.320
and land color instrument, and its sea and land surface temperature radiometer.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:08.880
The instruments are performing as expected for monitoring oceans, land, ice, and atmosphere.

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:15.280
A new simulation framework models chromatin organization at more than 10 times the previous spatial extent.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:21.260
It tracks how nucleosomes and histone modifications influence DNA accessibility and repair.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:26.940
The method allows researchers to examine longer genomic segments than earlier approaches permitted.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:33.500
All university chemists used operandospectroscopy to show that the active surface of nickel electrodes

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:40.300
in alkaline water electrolysis is nickel dioxide rather than the previously assumed nickel oxyhydroxide.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:46.260
The corrected structure appears in nature catalysis and revises decades of mechanistic assumptions.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:52.220
Tampere University researchers developed a compact lensless imager that fits inside standard

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:53.620
cell culture incubators.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:58.880
A single image yields quantitative data on cell growth and morphology without stains

00:05:58.880 --> 00:05:59.600
or labels.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:03.420
The system supports continuous monitoring for hours or days.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:08.420
Something most people get wrong is the idea that plants simply draw nitrogen from the

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:10.320
air the way they draw carbon dioxide.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:16.240
Atmospheric nitrogen gas stays inert until specialized microbes convert it into ammonia through

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:17.400
nitrogen fixation.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:23.520
The enzyme nitrogenase performs this conversion inside root nodules of legumes or in free-living

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:27.900
soil bacteria, and the process requires substantial energy from the microbes.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:33.400
A recent study identified a molecular off switch that bacteria use to halt fixation when

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.580
fixed nitrogen is already abundant nearby.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:41.420
That number matters because global agriculture applies more than 100 million tons of synthetic

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:45.620
nitrogen fertilizer each year, much of which runs off into waterways.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:51.040
Farmers could one day plant varieties that host microbes with tighter control over this switch,

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:53.860
Cutting fertilizer needs while maintaining yields.

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:58.820
Field trials testing whether edited crops retain the off-switch behavior without yield

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:02.220
loss are the next concrete step that would settle practical value.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:07.760
Before we go, field trials on edited crops that keep the nitrogen fixation off-switch are

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.660
expected in the coming growing season.

